  "description": "Householder planning application for the erection of rear roof terrace on second floor with associated composite privacy screening at the 1.8 metres of height and composite balustrades.\n\nThe heavy plastic (brown) decking is supported by a timber frame fixed to the exterior walls of the flat roof. There is no weight bearing on the roof itself. The frame is constructed of C24 145mm x 45mm treated kiln dried regularized timber. Beams to support the decking extend widthways across the full dimension of the roof. Under the decking the natural slant of the roof provides drainage into the adjacent guttering. The roof is further waterproofed with an additional bitumen coating.  \n\nThe composite privacy screening and balustrade are to be fixed to the timber frame, structure joists and to the brick wall using metal bolts and chemfix glue. ",
